# Syntropy's changes to the vendored ggml tree (`third_party/ggml/`), applied over the files of
# the upstream commit `third_party/ggml.lock` names. AGENTS.md's naming rule (D5) covers the
# vendored tree too, so these changes reword upstream comments and strings that name another
# project, and remove an optional CPU sub-backend, which the core builds without (RFC-0040 §8.1,
# note of 2026-10-31).
#
# Each section is an ed script, as `diff -e <upstream file> <vendored file>` writes it: line
# addresses and the new text only, never the text it replaces. Apply a section with
# `ed -s third_party/ggml/<path>`, giving it the script, then `w` and `q`. `ggml.lock` records the
# BLAKE3 of this file and of the tree before and after.
